\pard\qc\b\fs36\cf1 Sprint 3: Automation of Configuration Deployment\b0\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\qc\fs24\cf2 Presentation and Testing Evidence Document\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\qc\fs24\cf2 Project: React Config Lab\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\qc\fs24\cf2 Target Azure Key Vault: kv-hzb-c2-config\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 \par
\pard\pagebb\sa120
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Purpose\b0\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\sa100\fs22 This document explains how Sprint 3 was implemented and how each task can be tested. It is written for presentation use, so each section states the goal, the simple reason behind it, the test steps, and the expected result.\par
\pard\pagebb\sa120
\pard\b\fs28\cf1 Executive Summary\b0\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 - A GitHub Actions workflow deploys configuration to Azure Key Vault on approved push events.\par
\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 - Pull requests run validation only and do not deploy secrets.\par
\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 - Dummy configuration is used for safe pull request testing.\par
\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 - JSON validation prevents invalid or incomplete configuration from being deployed.\par
\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 - Azure CLI commands and a helper script verify stored secrets and versions.\par
\pard\pagebb\sa120
